1
00:00:25,123 --> 00:00:29,946
This is Notebook Companion: a voice-first study notebook for students, built on Gnani's speech models.

2
00:00:29,948 --> 00:00:31,778
Let me show you why it's worth switching to.

3
00:00:33,338 --> 00:00:34,938
Everyone gets their own private account.

4
00:00:34,968 --> 00:00:37,738
Pick a username and a password, and you land on a clean home page:

5
00:00:37,775 --> 00:00:42,775
a guided tour, a button for a new notebook, and one short notebook that explains what the app can do.

6
00:00:43,273 --> 00:00:45,988
Open a new notebook, tap the mic, and just talk.

7
00:00:52,888 --> 00:00:57,535
Gnani Prisma turns your speech into text, in English, ten Indian languages, or a mix of them,

8
00:00:57,563 --> 00:00:59,517
and your words appear on the page as neat notes.

9
00:00:59,982 --> 00:01:02,282
It's not only dictation. Ask it to write.

10
00:01:02,294 --> 00:01:04,717
A heading, a short summary, and a diagram:

11
00:01:05,705 --> 00:01:09,121
the AI writes the notes and draws the diagram right onto the sheet.

12
00:01:10,177 --> 00:01:12,892
Edit the same way. Change the heading to Food From Light.

13
00:01:13,132 --> 00:01:16,432
Changed your mind? Say undo. Every change can be taken back.

14
00:01:16,927 --> 00:01:19,112
The Companion knows every sheet of your notebook.

15
00:01:19,119 --> 00:01:24,119
Ask it anything, and it answers from your own notes, in short sentences that Gnani Timbre can read aloud.

16
00:01:24,971 --> 00:01:28,794
When it's time to revise, Study turns your notes into a quiz, with explanations.

17
00:01:28,812 --> 00:01:31,819
There are flashcards too, and a check of what your notes are missing.

18
00:01:32,437 --> 00:01:34,152
Upload your syllabus or slides.

19
00:01:34,176 --> 00:01:37,415
The app learns your course's own terms, so technical words are spelled right,

20
00:01:37,427 --> 00:01:40,142
and it shows how much of the syllabus your notes already cover.

21
00:01:40,942 --> 00:01:43,773
In class, Lecture mode records the whole lecture with live captions,

22
00:01:48,556 --> 00:01:51,795
then turns the transcript into organised notes, spread over new sheets.

23
00:01:52,575 --> 00:01:56,521
Your notes stay yours. Export them as PDF, Word or Markdown, any time.

24
00:01:57,175 --> 00:02:00,414
Notebook Companion. Just talk, and your notes write themselves.
